    "body": "## Problem\r\n\r\nGetting the current cursor position (the equivalent of `getpos('.')` or `nvim_win_get_cursor(0)`) as a `vim.Pos` requires specifying the mandatory `0` argument, which is inconsistent with most of the Lua stdlib, and is thus unintuitive.\r\n\r\n## Solution\r\n\r\nAllow for `vim.pos.cursor()` as shorthand for `vim.pos.cursor(0)`.\r\n\r\nI came to this idea independently while working with `vim.pos.cursor()` and finding the current behavior strange, but this idea was also proposed by @yochem [here](https://github.com/neovim/neovim/issues/39867#issuecomment-4481156550) (albeit before #40087).",
    "closed_at": "2026-07-28T11:21:45Z",
